# Required resource guidance

Every new resource page must include the shared, collapsed **About this resource**
card directly under its title, before its introduction and activity. This includes labs,
simulations, games, prototypes, readings and resource collections, whether authored
with Astro, React or standalone HTML.

Provide resource-specific answers to all three questions: what it is, how to use
its actual controls, and how it connects conceptually to LENS and learning
engineering. Include at least two practical use steps. Do not substitute slogans,
advertising or placeholders for conceptual connections.

Use `src/components/ResourceAbout.astro` or the shared renderer in
`src/lib/resource-about.mjs`. Keep keyboard access, native expanded-state semantics,
mobile layout and collapsed default behavior intact.

Every built HTML page is checked automatically. Never bypass the check by omitting
a page from a test list or adding a broad directory exception. Exact exceptions
in `src/data/resource-page-policy.json` need a specific, reviewed reason. Preserve
immutable research artifacts and provide guidance in their host pages.

Run `npm run build`, `npm run test:resource-guidance`,
`npm run test:resource-about`, and `npm run test:resource-about:browser`.
Both static and browser coverage are discovered from the completed build.
